            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-burgundy mb-6 uppercase tracking-wide">The Story</h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-ink mb-4 leading-relaxed">Vintage Politics brings together politics, journalism, public life and wine. Each guest reflects on the moments that shaped their life and career, with wines chosen to mark those defining years.</p>
            <p class="text-lg text-ink mb-4 leading-relaxed">The result is a different kind of conversation — one that moves beyond the usual soundbites to reveal the stories, memories and personalities behind public life.</p>
            <p class="text-lg text-ink mb-8 leading-relaxed">Every vintage tells a story. So does every guest.</p>
            
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-teal mb-3 uppercase tracking-wide border-t border-tan pt-6">Abbie Bennington</h2>
            <p class="text-ink leading-relaxed mb-4">Creator and host of Vintage Politics, Abbie is a journalist, broadcaster and wine expert. A former BBC News at Ten senior producer, she also worked alongside Nick Robinson during his time as BBC Political Editor.</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ink">
                <li>WSET Diploma holder</li>
                <li>Wine writer, educator and judge</li>
                <li>Chair of the Association of Wine Educators</li>
                <li>President of the London Tasting Awards 2026</li>
                <li>Bordeaux Wine School accredited tutor</li>
                <li>Rioja Educator</li>
                <li>Cava DO Advanced Educator</li>
            </ul>
